  "answer_core": "You shouldn’t grant Marcus 15% equity, a board seat, and a CTO title this week. Those are long‑term, hard‑to‑reverse commitments, and you still need evidence about whether his involvement reduces or concentrates risk.\n\nUse Friday to propose a clear, staged path. Tell him you’re open to major upside, but only after a short, defined window that proves what the partnership actually does for the company. Set a sprint that tests whether he can deliver the critical platform work, whether that work is revenue‑relevant, whether he stabilizes or destabilizes the team, whether knowledge transfer happens, and whether his behavior fits the governance you need. Be explicit about what successful performance in that window would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both premature commitments and a vague delay that might push him away. It gives him a real path tied to demonstrated impact, not hypothetical valuation math.",
